       §9The Curious 
      Christmas Elf
§3 ╚═--═ஓ๑⛇๑ஓ═--═╝

§1Sweetpea hesitated for only a moment. 

Her curiosity once again got the best of her... but this was no time for doubt.

A flick of her fingers,
#- §1and the ribbon unraveled, and the box opened on its own. A swirl of frost and light engulfed her.

Before she could even gasp, Sweetpea was flung into the biting cold of a snow-covered battlefield. 
The sound of roaring filled her ears!
#- §2“GET BACK, YOU                  FROSTED FIEND!”

§1A warrior woman, tall, imposing, yet graceful, green leaves and twigs blending within her silver armour, moving in the icy wind. She swung a massive sword with an ender eye in the hilt at a towering giant snow golem. 
#- §1The creature roared again, slamming it's colossal fists into the frozen ground, sending shockwaves that toppled nearby trees. 

Behind the warrior, 
an elf in gleaming purple robes and a long flowing green cape was casting spells with precision.
#- §1His hands weaving intricate patterns of light that struck the golem with bursts of fire and lightning.

Sweetpea blinked... 
There was no 
time to think! 
Acting on pure instinct, she extended her arm, and muttered an incantation. A storm of fiery sparks shot
#- §1from her fingertips, hitting the golem’s icy chest. It had been a while since she needed to use such defensive magic.

The elf prince turned, his long silver hair catching the light. His green eyes widened in surprise as he saw Sweetpea. §c“Who in the realms are you?”
#- §6“No time for introductions!” §1Sweetpea shouted.

The golem roared again, swiping it's massive arm toward them. Sweetpea leapt to the side, narrowly avoiding being crushed. She joined the prince, who was already crafting another spell.
#- §c“Well, whoever you are, you've got talent,”§1 the elf said, casting a shield to block an incoming icy blast. §c“I’m Castien. Let’s see what you’ve got, stranger.”

§1Sweetpea smirked. §6“Watch and learn, elf boy.” §1She sent a volley of glowing 
magic bolts causing
#- §1the golem to 
stumble back! 
Fern shouted from across the battlefield, §2“Less flirting, more fighting!” §1She charged at the monster with her sword. But the golem had tricks of it's own. It slammed both fists into the ground, sending a surge of freezing energy across the
#- §1battlefield. The ice beneath Sweetpea and Castien cracked, then shattered!

§c“Watch out!” §1Castien yelled, reaching for Sweetpea.

It was too late... 

The ice gave way, 
and they plunged 
into darkness.
#- §8*some time later*
§1Sweetpea groaned, her head pounding. The faint glow of Castien’s magic illuminated the icy walls of a small cave. Snow was packed above them, sealing the entrance. 
§c“Well, that’s unfortunate...” 
§1Castien said, brushing frost off his cloak.
#- §1He glanced at Sweetpea, his expression softening. §c“Oh good, you're awake. Are you hurt?”

§6“Just my pride,” §1she muttered, sitting up. She touched the snowy ceiling with her hand, muttering a spell to melt it, but nothing happened. Enchanted, resisting her magic.
#- §c“No use,” §1Castien said. §c“The golem’s magic is too strong. We’re stuck until Fern finishes the job.”
§1Sweetpea huffed and leaned back against the icy wall. §6“Perfect. Just perfect.”

§1Castien sat across from her, his eyes studying her curiously.
#- §c“You’re definitely not from around here, are you?”

§6“No,” §1Sweetpea said shortly.

§c“Care to elaborate?” §1Castien pressed, his tone playful.

Sweetpea sighed. §6“I was… investigating something. A promise
#- §6of answers, and then, poof, I’m here. Now I’m trapped in a cave with you instead of finding what I came for.”

§c“How dramatic!” 
§1Castien said 
with a smirk. 
Sweetpea shot him a glare. Despite herself, Sweetpea let out 
a small laugh. 
§6“You’re insufferable.” 
#- §c“I’ve been called worse,” §1Castien said. 

He stretched his 
long legs out, his expression turning more serious. 

§c"My father would 
be furious if he 
saw me like this.”

§6“Your father?”
#- §c“The King,” §1Castien said bitterly. §c“A cold, cruel man who thinks only of power. He expects perfection from me, his heir, and nothing less. I’ve spent my life trying to prove I’m more than his puppet, but…” §1He trailed off...

Sweetpea tilted her head. §6“But what?”
#- §c“But sometimes I think he’s right,” §1Castien admitted, his voice barely above a whisper. §c“No matter what I do, I’ll always be his shadow.”

§1Sweetpea frowned. 

§6“That’s ridiculous. You clearly have powerful magic, and you're... 
annoyingly likable.”
#- §c"A bit like you then stranger..." §1Castien said, his smirk returning. Sweetpea rolled her eyes.

Sweetpea’s thoughts wandered back to the mysterious promise that had brought her here in the first place. 

The gift lied.
#- §1The muffled roars of the golem stopped, leaving an uneasy silence. Sweetpea hugged her knees to her chest, the cold seeping into her bones. She glanced at Castien, who sat with his back against the icy wall, his expression dark. 
No sign of Fern or the outside world.
#- §6“It’s been too long,” §1Sweetpea muttered.

Castien gave a weak nod. §c“If Fern hasn’t shown up by now…” 
§1He trailed off, avoiding her gaze.

§6“I can’t just sit here! I didn’t come all this way to freeze to death in a cave 
with an elf!"
#- §c"A powerful mage..." §1Castien corrected, though his voice lacked it's usual levity. Instead, there was an edge to it that Sweetpea hadn’t heard before.
She looked up at him and their eyes met.
Castien hesitated, running a hand through his silver hair. 
#- §c“I’ve studied… other kinds of magic. Magic that could get us out of here. But…”

§6“But what?” 
§1Sweetpea pressed.

§c“It’s dangerous,” §1Castien admitted. 

Sweetpea narrowed her eyes. §c“Dark magic. Forbidden spells..."
#- §c"Things I was never supposed to learn, but I did anyway. Because sometimes, power is the only way ...to survive.”

§1Sweetpea felt a chill that had nothing to do with the ice around them. 

§c"I studied every kind of magic I could find,
#- §cincluding the kind my father forbade. If I really wanted too...
I could break enchantments like this. I even know how to cheat death itself.”

§6“Cheat death?” §1Sweetpea repeated, her voice barely above a whisper.

§c“Immortality!”
#- §c“It’s possible, but it comes at the cost of your soul. A price I swore I’d never pay."

§1Sweetpea stared at him, her mind racing. The charming elf prince suddenly seemed far more complicated than she had realised. §6“You’d actually use that 
kind of magic?"
#- §c“Not just to get out,” §1Castien said. §c“To protect Fern. To stop that golem. To make sure no one else suffers.” §1He leaned forward, his expression intense. §c“I’ve spent my life trying to prove I’m more than just my father’s shadow. Maybe this is 
how I do it?”
#- §1For a moment, neither of them spoke. The silence was heavy, oppressive.

Before Sweetpea could respond, a thunderous crash echoed above them, followed by the unmistakable sound 
of Fern’s voice.

§2        “Hold on!”
#- §1Sweetpea and Castien looked at each other, now much more curiously. 

Fern’s sword broke through the barrier. Light flooded the cave. 

§2“Thought I’d lost you two!” §1she called, offering her hand 
to Castien.
#- §1He snapped back into character. §c“Not a chance,” §1he said, pulling himself up.

He turned to 
Sweetpea and extended his hand. §c“Coming stranger?”

§1Sweetpea took it. 
A strange pull 
tugged at her... 
§6“WAIT!” §1she shouted!
#- §1The world spun around her, and in the blink of an eye, she was back home in her tavern.

Sweetpea’s chest heaved as she struggled to process what had happened. 

§6“No, no, no!” §1she cried, slamming her hands 
on the desk.
#- §1The memory of Castien’s dark confession lingered in her mind. She paced the room, muttering to herself. §6“Dark magic? Immortality? Who is that elf?” §1she muttered.

§6He could be the key 
to our survival.
§5§oThat is who I was afraid of my dear.§r
#- §k00101100010110000101010101010101010101010101010101010100101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010010101010101010101010101010101010101101010101010101101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101101010101010101010101010101010
#- §6Oh my... you scared me!§r
§5You opened the gift didn't you? 🤨§r
§6I'm sorry, I just had to see what...§r
§5I can't trust you now!§r
§6Oh come on...§r              §5What did you find?§r
§6I found us a way 
out of this mess! 😏§r
§5The Lanterns will...§r
§6NO!§r §cCastien§r §6will!§r 
§6He knows how 
to become immortal!§r 
#- §5No way! You are not 
to go anywhere near that man do you understand me!§r
§6I helped save his life, and he helped me...§r
§5§lSweetpea stop!§r§r
§6I saw his power, he told me what he could do, and we don't have any time left to do 
this our way!§r
§5We still have time...§r
§6§lNO WE DON'T!§r§r
#- §k00101100010110000101010101010101010101010101010101010100101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010010101010101010101010101010101010101101010101010101101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101101010101010101010101010101010
#-       §8{flashback}§r

§1The grand hall was silent as Castien stood before King Theron, his father’s cold haunting eyes fixed on him.§r

§4“You met a woman...”§r 

§1Theron said slowly, 
his voice sharp and measured.§r 
#- §4“Sweetpea, you called her. And you claim she’s powerful?”§r

§c“Yes,” §1Castien replied. §c“She’s unlike anyone I’ve seen. She fought alongside us...”

§4“And you didn’t 
bring her to me?” 
§1Theron’s tone dropped, icy and dangerous.
#- §c“She’s no threat,” §1Castien said firmly.

The King descended from his throne, 
each step deliberate. Without warning, he struck Castien across the face, the blow ringing in the vast chamber.

§4“You are a fool,” §1Theron hissed. 
#- §4“Power like hers doesn’t go unnoticed. She will serve us. 
And if not... we take her power. And you let her slip away!”

§1Castien’s cheek burned, but his voice remained steady. 

§c“If she’s as powerful as you think, she’ll come back."
#- §1Theron’s gaze darkened. §4“If she does, you will bring her to me. Do not fail me again, Castien.”

§1Castien said nothing
as his father left.

§c§o“Maybe you should 
be worried about 
what she was searching for...”§r 
§1Castien thought.
